1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,545
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:06,673
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,971
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,726 --> 00:00:19,144
[Lily, in English] <i>I don't know who he is.</i>
<i>I told you.</i>

7
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:20,353
[Lily, in English] <i>I've never met him</i>
<i>in my entire life!</i>

8
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,730
[in English] You are lying!

9
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:23,898
[Atoy, in English]
<i>We are not working together.</i>

10
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:26,568
[in English] Where is the laptop?

11
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:28,111
- Mmm.
- [grunts]

12
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:28,903
[Lily, in English] No, no, no, no, no!

13
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:31,156
[Audrey] You need to be taken
to the hospital. Gavin!

14
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:32,282
[Dmitri, in English] <i>Promise me.</i>

15
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>You won't do anything</i>
<i>with what you've learned.</i>

16
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:37,454
[in English] And where is my briefcase?

17
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:39,497
- [both grunt]
- [wailing]

18
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:42,667
I'm sorry if this trip is sudden.

19
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,462
[Audrey] <i>But we need to see</i>
<i>your Daddy Atoy first.</i>

20
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:46,880
No one leaves.

21
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:48,339
[Red] Try to start that.

22
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:50,508
[in English] I need you
to report to me in person.

23
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:52,427
[in English] Padua is compromised.

24
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:54,304
[Audrey] <i>We're going to see Dad</i>
<i>at the hospital.</i>

25
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:56,139
Hospital, but you're bringing luggage?

26
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:58,767
You even brought this evidence
that could ruin your family.

27
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:00,185
[in English] Please.
Please, just let us go.

28
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:02,312
PREVIOUSLY

29
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,731
[Martina] <i>Get a gag</i>
<i>and ropes for these two.</i>

30
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:06,691
And no one should know they're here.

31
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:09,360
[Ibyang] <i>I just want to understand her.</i>

32
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:11,154
<i>Does Mama have another child?</i>

33
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:12,781
Where is she?

34
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:16,201
Sam, Sam, my child! Sam!

35
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:18,912
- [Charmi] <i>She's your sibling.</i>
- Sammy, Sammy!

36
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,497
- [Audrey wailing]
- [Mongki] Good night again.

37
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:24,042
[wailing and muttering]

38
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:32,759
[music fades]

39
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:36,513
They're secured, boss.
I made sure they're sleeping soundly.

40
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,264
[in English] Good.

41
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:41,643
Boss, what if Sir Dmitri comes home?

42
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:45,730
How do we explain to him that Audrey
and his grandchild are missing?

43
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:48,775
He has already arrived. I spoke to him.

44
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:54,030
I told him his precious daughter
and grandchild suddenly left,

45
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:55,657
and it looks like they're not coming back.

46
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,325
So, he's upset.

47
00:01:58,451 --> 00:01:59,702
[Mongki] By the way, boss.

48
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:02,163
My men tracked Paldo.

49
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,957
They know where he's hiding.

50
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,544
[suspicious music playing]

51
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:08,878
Put him to sleep too.

52
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,131
Make sure he never wakes up.

53
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,759
[Mongki, in English] Copy, boss.

54
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,430
[line rings]

55
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:20,890
We have the go signal.

56
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:24,644
Shoot them and make sure it's clean.

57
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:27,939
[foreboding music playing]

58
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:37,907
[music fades]

59
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,704
[clicks tongue]

60
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:44,038
[sighs]

61
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:46,291
Life goes on. [inhales]

62
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,002
Life goes on.

63
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:04,767
[ominous music playing]

64
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:17,655
[tense music playing]

65
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:28,625
[both gasp]

66
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,419
Oh? Paldo.

67
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:34,339
What are you doing there, bro?

68
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:35,757
- Oh?
- Emerson.

69
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,551
Come here. What's happening to you?

70
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,178
Bro…

71
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:42,138
Bro, they're still chasing me.

72
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:44,849
I don't want to die yet, bro.

73
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:47,602
[in English] Please, please.

74
00:03:47,685 --> 00:03:50,480
Hide me. Hide me here.

75
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:51,940
Please, I beg you, bro.

76
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:53,358
[whimpering]

77
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:54,901
Bro, they'll kill me.

78
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:58,863
- Man, they'll kill me. Please?
- [muttering]

79
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:01,950
- Please, help me.
- Yes, yes, yes. Okay, okay, okay.

80
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,785
- I'm scared.
- Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

81
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:05,370
I'll handle it, I'll handle it.

82
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,455
[suave theme music playing]

83
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,190
- Guys, guys! You know…
- [Bunda, in English] Yes?

84
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,108
I have a secret for you.

85
00:04:35,191 --> 00:04:35,900
- What?
- Wow.

86
00:04:35,984 --> 00:04:37,026
- I just want to share.
- [muttering]

87
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,529
I'll try a gimmick later at my eatery.

88
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:40,905
- [all] Ohh!
- Secret?

89
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,448
- Why did you tell us?
- Secret--

90
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:44,409
- It's a secret!
- Now we know!

91
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:45,743
- As if--
- Do you like lechon?

92
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,620
- Of course!
- Oh! I love that!

93
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:48,454
[muttering]

94
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,248
- What if you add more serving--
- [horn honking]

95
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:51,249
[squeals]

96
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:52,166
- San Antonio de Padua!
- [horn honking]

97
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:53,126
- [screaming]
- [tense music playing]

98
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:54,419
[clamoring]

99
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,421
[Bunda] Get back here!

100
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:58,673
- [Bunda] You don't own this road!
- Hey!

101
00:04:58,756 --> 00:05:00,842
[Mona] Next time, slow down!

102
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:02,176
[ominous music playing]

103
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,094
[thug 1] Are you sure about this?

104
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:04,554
[thug 2] I'm sure, boss. It's here.

105
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:07,765
[gasping]

106
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:09,100
- [guns cock]
- [squeals]

107
00:05:09,684 --> 00:05:12,478
[screaming and panicking]

108
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:18,776
Let's go already!

109
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,863
[Siony] Come on, before-- Come on, I said!

110
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:24,073
- [gunshots blasting]
- [screaming and panicking]

111
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:28,453
[molotov shattering]

112
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:31,247
[gunshots blasting]

113
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:32,123
[Emerson gasps]

114
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:33,750
- Criminals!
- [muttering]

115
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,918
Leave Emerson alone! [grunts]

116
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,171
[thug 1] Let's go! Run!

117
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:40,048
- [clattering]
- [shrieking]

118
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:41,007
- [Siony] Wait.
- [grunts]

119
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:43,968
- I'll call the police!
- Quick, sis! Call now!

120
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:45,595
[thug 2] Go!

121
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:46,971
[Bunda] Let's go attack them!

122
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:49,182
- Hurry! Attack!
- [shrieking]

123
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:51,434
[Bunda] Let's call
the fire department too!

124
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,811
- [shrieking]
- [Siony] Come on!

125
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,188
Let's get out!

126
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:57,815
What do you want?
Burn alive inside or get shot outside?!

127
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,818
- [coughs]
- You go first.

128
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:04,113
- [coughing]
- [fire crackling]

129
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:09,243
[music fades]

130
00:06:09,994 --> 00:06:11,662
Mama, where are we going?

131
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:14,040
Shh! Can't you see I'm talking?

132
00:06:14,123 --> 00:06:17,585
[phone ringing]

133
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:19,879
What?

134
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:21,380
[in English] Hello, madam.

135
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:24,884
Uh, are you on your way to the café?
Are you there already?

136
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,344
Oh. [titters]

137
00:06:26,427 --> 00:06:29,138
[in English] I'm, I'm… I'm sorry.
I-I forgot.

138
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,015
Uh, what do you need?

139
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,308
[Martina on the phone] <i>Money?</i>

140
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:33,518
<i>You got paid already, right?</i>

141
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:35,144
Uh…

142
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:37,855
[somber music playing]

143
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,649
Because, um…

144
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:41,984
Can you take the child from me now?

145
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,029
[Olga on phone] <i>I don't want</i>
<i>to do this anymore.</i>

146
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:47,115
I'm already annoyed with her.

147
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:48,616
She's too meddlesome.

148
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,743
[in English] Excuse me?

149
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,620
[in English] You don't tell us what to do.

150
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:55,289
We'll tell you when to return the child.

151
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,333
[in English] So, just deal with her. Okay?

152
00:06:57,416 --> 00:06:58,793
[pensive music playing]

153
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,802
[sighs]

154
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:09,053
Damn.

155
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:12,348
This is insane! Let's go!

156
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,225
Mama, wait.

157
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:16,561
Who were you talking to?

158
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:19,856
- [heavy music playing]
- [Emerson groans]

159
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:21,732
- [Paldo] Help us!
- [Emerson coughs]

160
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:24,360
- [Emerson] Help.
- [coughing]

161
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:26,487
- [coughing]
- [people screaming outside]

162
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,697
[Paldo] Help us!

163
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,866
- [screaming]
- Oh my God! Oh, no!

164
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:32,577
- Emerson's Tailoring Shop is burning!
- [screaming]

165
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,662
- Emerson!
- [coughs]

166
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:35,580
[Paldo] Help us!

167
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,541
- My gosh! It's burning!
- Emerson, I'll save you!

168
00:07:38,624 --> 00:07:39,459
Wait, wait!

169
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:42,128
- [screaming and panicking]
- Emerson!

170
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:43,337
Ah, move back!

171
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:44,964
Emong, tell them to move back!

172
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:47,675
[screaming and panicking]

173
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:49,385
[Emong] Help!

174
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:51,512
- [man 1] We need firefighters!
- [man 2] Firefighters!

175
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:55,349
- [screaming and panicking]
- [Denden] Firefighters!

176
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:57,185
- Water!
- Water!

177
00:07:58,769 --> 00:07:59,854
Neighbors!

178
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:02,857
I'm sure those outsiders
won't return here anymore.

179
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,442
After what we did?

180
00:08:04,525 --> 00:08:06,360
They'll never come back!

181
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:08,321
- They're so arrogant, but no guts.
- Correct!

182
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:12,742
[phone ringing]

183
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,164
I'm just reminding you…

184
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:19,081
[pensive music playing]

185
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,917
He's Red Regalia's son.

186
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,919
[Cita] He's the one
who killed your father.

187
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:25,379
He already clashed with Atoy.

188
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:29,050
Who knows, maybe his dad
sent him over to spy around here?

189
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:30,676
To get revenge on Atoy.

190
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,930
Don't be swayed
by his smiles and cuteness,

191
00:08:34,013 --> 00:08:35,389
even if he's your friend.

192
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:37,350
[phone ringing]

193
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:38,309
[T-Bak] Hey!

194
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:40,061
That's Gavin!

195
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:41,687
Why did you reject him?

196
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:43,564
[somber music playing]

197
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,024
[T-Bak] Rejected?

198
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:46,317
[screaming and panicking]

199
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,652
- Fire!
- [screaming and panicking]

200
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:49,862
[clamoring]

201
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,697
[woman] Fire!

202
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:54,784
[screaming and panicking]

203
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:58,329
[all] Help! Help!

204
00:08:58,412 --> 00:09:00,373
[Paldo] Help! Please help us!

205
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:04,627
[screaming and panicking]

206
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:09,590
Make way! They're still inside!

207
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:11,842
Stay back!

208
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:13,844
Let me go! The fire is getting bigger!

209
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:16,597
- [Paldo] Help!
- [screaming and panicking]

210
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:17,640
[Paldo] Help!

211
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:21,269
- [Kurt] Paldo! Paldo! Paldo!
- [panicking]

212
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:25,690
- [Paldo] Help!
- [coughing]

213
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,942
[Kurt] Hey, hey! Wait, wait, wait, wait!

214
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:29,151
[Emerson groans]

215
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:31,237
[Kurt] Okay, okay. Go, go, go.

216
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,905
[Paldo] Emerson too! Ouch!

217
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:37,118
[screaming and panicking]

218
00:09:37,201 --> 00:09:39,328
- Paldo!
- Brother Paldo!

219
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:41,455
[Emerson] Help! Help!

220
00:09:41,539 --> 00:09:43,499
- [Kurt] Emerson!
- [Emerson] Help!

221
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:46,043
- [Kurt] Emerson! Where are you?!
- [indistinct shouting]

222
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,920
- [Kurt grunts]
- [Emerson coughs]

223
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:50,423
- Here, here, that's it.
- [grunts]

224
00:09:50,506 --> 00:09:51,340
[Kurt, in English] I got you, bro.

225
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:52,508
- [Emong] Water!
- [Kurt] I got you. I got you!

226
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:53,801
- [coughing]
- [screaming and panicking]

227
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:55,386
- [Kurt] Okay, go.
- [Emerson] Hurry with the water!

228
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:58,556
[Kurt] Come on, come on.
I got you, I got you. There!

229
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:00,224
[music fades]

230
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:02,435
Can we watch a movie?

231
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:03,603
[scoffs] Well.

232
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,438
What do you think you are? Lucky?

233
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:07,773
No! Let's go home!

234
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,358
You'll just make me spend money.

235
00:10:12,069 --> 00:10:13,321
What?

236
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:15,114
Why are you standing there?

237
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:16,657
Come on!

238
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:18,784
[pensive music playing]

239
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:23,164
Mama, I already said sorry to you.

240
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:28,586
But why do you still seem angry with me?

241
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:33,257
If I had known that toy belonged
to Sister Sammy,

242
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:36,260
I wouldn't have touched it.

243
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:42,141
Don't mention Sammy, okay.

244
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:43,809
Because you don't know her!

245
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,394
Do you understand?

246
00:10:50,274 --> 00:10:53,402
Because you never tell me about her!

247
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:58,199
Wait. I don't understand you.

248
00:10:58,282 --> 00:11:01,869
Didn't you say you wanted to be with me?

249
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:05,331
But why does it feel like you
don't want me?

250
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:06,540
[sobs]

251
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:11,337
I'm doing everything to be close to you.

252
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,339
[sobs]

253
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,092
Do you know why?

254
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:17,426
Huh?

255
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:22,223
Because I love Sammy more than you!

256
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:25,184
That's why I gave you away, right?

257
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:27,311
Huh? Come on! Let's go!

258
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:28,479
Come on.

259
00:11:28,562 --> 00:11:29,855
- [Emerson coughs]
- [Kurt] Take him.

260
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,732
- [coughing]
- [screaming and panicking]

261
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:36,404
[clamoring]

262
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:41,283
Wait! Emerson!

263
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:43,577
- Emerson, Emerson!
- [screaming and panicking]

264
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:48,040
[Bunda] What do we do?!

265
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,083
I don't know how!

266
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:51,419
- Huh? I'll do it! I'll do it!
- [Denden] I don't know how!

267
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:52,962
I can do this. I can do this.

268
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:55,089
CPR and mouth-to-mouth resuscitation.

269
00:11:55,172 --> 00:11:57,716
[music swells]

270
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,679
[coughs]

271
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:03,722
[exclaims]

272
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:09,895
[shrieking, laughing, cheering]

273
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,439
He woke up!

274
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:13,357
[T-Bak] There! The firefighters are here!

275
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:14,984
[exclaiming]

276
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:48,809
[upbeat rock music playing]

277
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:56,442
[music fades]

278
00:12:56,525 --> 00:12:58,110
Ah, it hurts!

279
00:12:58,194 --> 00:12:59,945
- Let's go!
- Ma, it hurts!

280
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,780
Stop it. Stop your crying already.

281
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:03,365
[sobbing] Mommy!

282
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:06,202
- Ma!
- Come on!

283
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:07,828
[shrieks]

284
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:09,747
It hurts!

285
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:11,373
It hurts!

286
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:12,541
[Olga grunts]

287
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:16,921
Why did you even come back for me?!

288
00:13:17,004 --> 00:13:18,339
[melodramatic music playing]

289
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:21,717
I wish you weren't my mother!

290
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:25,179
Just give me back to Tatoy!

291
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,723
[sobs] You're a bad mother!

292
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:32,645
I'm not a bad mother!
I didn't want what happened!

293
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:35,231
I love Sammy so much!

294
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:38,025
Do you understand? She's my life!

295
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:39,610
Do you understand me?!

296
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:43,614
- Do you understand me?!
- [wails, then grunts]

297
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:47,785
[squeals]

298
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:49,453
[epic music playing]

299
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:50,621
[thudding]

300
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:51,622
Mama!

301
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:53,666
[music swells]

302
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:56,335
[pensive music playing]

303
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:58,462
- [tense sinister music playing]
- [Olga groans]

304
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:00,798
[Ibyang] Ma. Mama?

305
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:02,216
I'm okay.

306
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:04,051
[gasping]

307
00:14:04,134 --> 00:14:04,969
I'm okay.

308
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,098
I'm okay.

309
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:18,566
Emerson, don't think about the things
you lost inside anymore.

310
00:14:19,149 --> 00:14:20,818
At least nothing happened to you.

311
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:23,153
Many of us will help you out.

312
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:24,989
[somber music playing]

313
00:14:25,072 --> 00:14:29,368
[indistinct chattering]

314
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:31,370
- [Mona] Who could have done that?
- [woman] It's terrible.

315
00:14:31,453 --> 00:14:32,872
Sorry, bro.

316
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,623
[indistinct chattering]

317
00:14:34,707 --> 00:14:37,501
- [woman 1] He's so handsome! Wait.
- [woman 2] Such a nice nose.

318
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:39,128
[women shrieking]

319
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:41,505
Thanks to all of you. Wait!

320
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:43,924
Ah! Have we met before?

321
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:45,050
Where?

322
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:46,677
In my dream.

323
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,012
[giggling, shrieking]

324
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:49,930
[Karla] Such a flirt! Wow!

325
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:53,017
He's so handsome!
Probably even more if shirtless!

326
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:56,520
- [giggling]
- Hey! Show us your abs!

327
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:57,646
Stop it!

328
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,523
Look at mine instead.

329
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:02,359
- Why?
- Wow! Look who's talking!

330
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,528
You look like Adamus,

331
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:07,865
the guardian of the water gem
in <i>Encantadia</i>!

332
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:09,283
- Oh, yes!
- Yes!

333
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:11,076
- [Bunda] Yes, right?
- [Mona] Doesn't he?

334
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,453
That's too much.

335
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:13,621
No, no. I din't look like him.

336
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:15,247
He's too handsome compared to me.

337
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,416
You're saying too much!

338
00:15:17,499 --> 00:15:19,543
- Don't you know him?
- No. Who is he?

339
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:21,670
He's Uno Alcaraz!

340
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,881
[Siony] One of our
volunteer firefighters here!

341
00:15:23,964 --> 00:15:26,050
- Uno!
- Volunteer!

342
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:27,760
Wow! [cheering]

343
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:29,345
Great job! Thank you!

344
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:30,763
[applauding]

345
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,933
[Bunda] Thank you.

346
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,851
So, you're a volunteer?

347
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:37,061
[in English] Yes, miss.

348
00:15:37,561 --> 00:15:39,980
So, you're not a real firefighter?
Just a volunteer?

349
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,565
[pleasant music playing]

350
00:15:42,441 --> 00:15:46,820
What do you do when there's no fire?

351
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,783
I'm not like regular firefighters

352
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,370
who are paid for their work.

353
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:56,872
Even if I'm just a volunteer,

354
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:59,583
I'm trained and reliable.

355
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:03,045
Always ready to help when there's a fire.

356
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:05,923
And if you have problems,

357
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,467
as long as not financial ones…

358
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:09,551
[smirks]

359
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:11,303
I'm here too.

360
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:13,138
- [Bunda] Yes!
- [Siony] Wow!

361
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:15,432
- Us, us.
- [Siony] Thank you.

362
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:18,310
- [Mona] So sweet. Thank you.
- We're always ready to help you.

363
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:21,397
But you still haven't
answered my question.

364
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:25,275
What's your job
when you're not volunteering?

365
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:27,069
[pleasant music playing]

366
00:16:31,281 --> 00:16:32,116
[music fades]

367
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:41,208
[Olga moans]

368
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:43,585
[groans]

369
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:45,462
I'll do it.

370
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:46,630
[clicks tongue]

371
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:47,840
How are you, Ma?

372
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:48,799
Ouch.

373
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:50,217
- Are you hurt?
- [groans]

374
00:16:52,219 --> 00:16:53,387
Ouch! [groans]

375
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:57,307
[grunts] Everything hurts.

376
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,308
Ouch,

377
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,727
Oh God.

378
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:03,063
Feels like my hips will break.

379
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,857
- [sighs]
- [somber music playing]

380
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:05,941
You?

381
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:09,528
Are you okay?

382
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:13,157
Weren't you hurt?

383
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:15,117
No.

384
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:18,328
You saved me.

385
00:17:18,412 --> 00:17:20,039
[melancholic music playing]

386
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:22,875
You got hurt because of me.

387
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:23,917
[sighs]

388
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,794
[in English] Sorry.

389
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:28,964
[music fades]

390
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,716
Karla! What's this?

391
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:32,051
[in English] <i>Fast Talk with Boy Abunda?</i>

392
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,135
[Mona] Exactly.

393
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:37,181
Baby Uno, if a dog chased me here,

394
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:39,058
would you help me?

395
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:41,977
- Of course, definitely.
- [Bunda] Oh! He'll help you!

396
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:45,314
- Come here, come here, come here.
- [Bunda] Hey. What's that?

397
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,484
Ms. Karla. Right?

398
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:49,818
[pleasant music playing]

399
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:52,821
If you also want
to be a volunteer firefighter,

400
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,656
just tell me.

401
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:58,410
I'll help you join our team.

402
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:01,455
- [Bunda] Ah.
- Wait, wait, wait!

403
00:18:01,538 --> 00:18:02,998
Why is she the only one invited?

404
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,209
Uh…

405
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:06,668
I mean…

406
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:10,672
all of us can be volunteers.

407
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:13,383
We don't choose.

408
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:16,303
I'll volunteer, volunteer!

409
00:18:16,386 --> 00:18:18,013
I'll volunteer!

410
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:20,182
- [Siony] Stop interfering.
- [Bunda] I'll fight you for that.

411
00:18:20,265 --> 00:18:22,601
Stop butting in,
because we already have a winner.

412
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:25,104
- Who?
- And that's Karla!

413
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:27,022
[teasing and cheering]

414
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:30,359
- [T-Bak] Hey, Karla!
- [Bunda] Stop it!

415
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:31,985
[teasing and exclaiming]

416
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,202
[somber music playing]

417
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,037
[alcohol spritzing]

418
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:47,417
[gasps]

419
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:48,585
Ow.

420
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,963
Ma, you should see a doctor.

421
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:52,548
Wait. I'll call Sister…

422
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:54,091
Uh, no need.

423
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:57,594
That's just extra expense. Sit down here.

424
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,768
I thought you didn't want me anymore?

425
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:06,895
Because I'm a bad mother.

426
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:11,108
I can't leave you alone.

427
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:15,779
Jeez.

428
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:21,869
I saved you,
that's why you can't leave me.

429
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:24,746
You feel guilty leaving me alone.

430
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,210
That's okay. I deserve it.

431
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,921
No.

432
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,550
I'm here because

433
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:39,386
you are my mama.

434
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:43,348
I felt it when

435
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,601
you chose to save me.

436
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:50,564
[smooching]

437
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:55,110
I'm here, Mama.

438
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,909
I won't leave you.

439
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:04,119
I'll watch over you.

440
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,331
[in English] Promise!

441
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:11,752
I won't be naughty or stubborn anymore,

442
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:14,338
so

443
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:16,715
you won't get angry.

444
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:25,641
[Olga] <i>What the hell?!</i>

445
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:28,685
Sammy! This is so annoying--

446
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:33,774
Didn't I tell you after playing,
you should clean up your own toys?!

447
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:36,151
What is this? You're so messy!

448
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,695
Oh my. This child!

449
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:42,199
Unbelievable! It even reached the table!

450
00:20:42,824 --> 00:20:44,326
It's so messy.

451
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:46,203
Oh!

452
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:51,792
What is this?!

453
00:20:51,875 --> 00:20:52,960
Sammy!

454
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,338
Why are you so dirty?!

455
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:58,090
Oh my!

456
00:20:59,883 --> 00:21:02,803
If the neighbors see you, your appearance!

457
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:05,055
They'll say I'm neglecting you!

458
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,181
Oh!

459
00:21:06,723 --> 00:21:09,559
- [somber music playing]
- [gulps]

460
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:19,152
[smooches]

461
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:21,405
Mama, I'm sorry.

462
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:23,490
Please don't be mad.

463
00:21:23,573 --> 00:21:24,408
[sobs]

464
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:26,368
[Sammy] I'll fix my toys,

465
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:29,204
and I'll change my clothes.

466
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:31,957
[smooches]

467
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,252
Please forgive me.

468
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:37,879
[in English] Mama, sorry.

469
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:39,881
[in English] Mama, sorry. [sobs]

470
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:43,427
I didn't mean it, Mama.

471
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,678
[in English] Sorry.

472
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:47,889
[sobs] Please forgive me.

473
00:21:48,473 --> 00:21:49,891
[sobs] Mommy.

474
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,562
[in English] Mama, please.

475
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:55,605
[in English] Sorry, Mama.

476
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:58,859
Stop crying, Sammy.

477
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:02,404
Mama isn't angry anymore.

478
00:22:03,613 --> 00:22:07,034
[melodramatic music playing]

479
00:22:22,049 --> 00:22:22,924
[sighs]

480
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:33,935
Oh, take it slowly.

481
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:35,312
[chuckles softly]

482
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:41,735
Hmm.

483
00:22:42,569 --> 00:22:43,528
It's delicious.

484
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,572
- You're good!
- Yes!

485
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:48,533
I knew you'd like it!

486
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:50,702
One more, Mama.

487
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:53,163
Here, try the chicken.

488
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:54,206
[chuckles softly]

489
00:22:55,123 --> 00:22:57,417
[pleasant music playing]

490
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:10,931
[music fades]

491
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:13,892
Ibyang.

492
00:23:15,602 --> 00:23:17,813
Why are you still kind to me?

493
00:23:18,897 --> 00:23:20,232
Even though…

494
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:25,529
you know, I'm a bit harsh with you.

495
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,615
You still didn't leave me.

496
00:23:29,616 --> 00:23:33,787
Because you're my mama.

497
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:36,706
You're my family,

498
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:39,000
and with family,

499
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,419
no one gets left behind.

500
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:47,175
[somber music playing]

501
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,233
Aren't you…

502
00:24:05,318 --> 00:24:07,279
curious about Sammy?

503
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:15,954
Here she is.

504
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:30,218
Her favorite dish
was adobo with coconut milk.

505
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:36,141
She didn't like candies, but…

506
00:24:36,892 --> 00:24:38,643
she loved native rice cakes.

507
00:24:41,688 --> 00:24:43,607
Her favorite colors…

508
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:48,904
Purple and…

509
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:50,864
sky blue.

510
00:24:50,947 --> 00:24:52,324
[sobs]

511
00:24:54,117 --> 00:24:57,913
She loved it when I braided her hair.

512
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:04,461
[sobbing]

513
00:25:05,503 --> 00:25:08,715
Stop crying. Stop crying.

514
00:25:13,011 --> 00:25:14,221
You know…

515
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:19,142
You're lucky, because…

516
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:22,062
you still got to be with her.

517
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:26,274
But me, I didn't.

518
00:25:30,654 --> 00:25:34,407
But I'll behave better…

519
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:39,454
so you won't be upset with me.

520
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:46,753
I'll do everything to make you happy.

521
00:25:48,838 --> 00:25:53,093
So Sister Sammy won't worry anymore.

522
00:26:03,853 --> 00:26:06,231
[groans] Ouch.

523
00:26:06,982 --> 00:26:08,275
[groans]

524
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:13,363
- Ma, can you stand up now?
- Oh?

525
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:18,576
Um, my hips still hurt a bit.

526
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,496
But don't worry.

527
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:23,581
I'm fine.

528
00:26:24,457 --> 00:26:27,335
Better go upstairs.

529
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:28,712
You should rest now.

530
00:26:28,795 --> 00:26:30,380
Go to sleep.

531
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:31,798
Hmm?

532
00:26:33,341 --> 00:26:34,259
Yes.

533
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:37,554
But finish this, okay.

534
00:26:37,637 --> 00:26:39,055
- Yes!
- Hmm.

535
00:26:39,139 --> 00:26:40,473
[chuckles softly]

536
00:26:41,933 --> 00:26:42,809
Go on.

537
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:45,145
[in English] Good night, Ma.

538
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:46,938
[in English] Good night, Ibyang.

539
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:49,107
[sniffles]

540
00:26:49,190 --> 00:26:50,650
[sentimental music playing]

541
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:51,735
[smooches]

542
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,781
Careful on the stairs, okay.

543
00:26:56,865 --> 00:26:57,866
Yes.

544
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:18,011
[tense music playing]

545
00:27:19,471 --> 00:27:21,097
- [Janine grunts]
- Child, untie me.

546
00:27:21,181 --> 00:27:23,183
- Quick, hurry. Child, child!
- [Janine panting]

547
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:25,060
[guttural cry of pain]

548
00:27:25,143 --> 00:27:27,270
- [Red] What, huh?! Huh?!
- [Audrey] What will you do to her?!

549
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:29,064
- [Red] You'll escape?!
- [Audrey] Don't hurt her!

550
00:27:29,147 --> 00:27:30,148
- Mommy!
- Take her!

551
00:27:30,231 --> 00:27:31,066
- Let me go!
- [Audrey sobs]

552
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:33,943
- Take her!
- Enough! Let go of my child!

553
00:27:34,027 --> 00:27:35,528
- Let her go!
- [Red] Take them there!

554
00:27:35,612 --> 00:27:37,113
UP NEXT

555
00:27:37,197 --> 00:27:39,616
[grunts]

556
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:41,242
You'll shoot me because of Audrey?

557
00:27:42,577 --> 00:27:46,706
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

558
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:52,337
[in English] I will make you talk.

559
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:55,757
[in English] You see,
men like you have families.

560
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:59,469
[in English] I have men right now

561
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:02,514
searching for all of your beloved.

562
00:28:02,597 --> 00:28:07,394
[in English] And I will kill every
one of them right in front of your face.

563
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:09,187
- <i>♪ Holding the scissors</i> ♪
- [groans]

564
00:28:09,270 --> 00:28:12,565
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

565
00:28:12,649 --> 00:28:14,526
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

566
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:17,028
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
